This works nicely if the onRender is within renderLeaflet(). However, if I move the onRender() to a leafletProxy() reacting to an actionButton, it doesn't seem to work. Is there any way around this? Below is an example with a simple onRender() with no additional plugin

Thanks

This works:

library(leaflet)
library(shiny)
library(htmlwidgets)

runApp(list(ui=pageWithSidebar(
  headerPanel=("Example"),
  sidebarPanel(
    actionButton("go", label="Go")
  ),
  mainPanel(
    leafletOutput("map"))
  ),
server=function(input, output, session){
  output$map <- renderLeaflet({
    leaflet(quakes)  %>%
      addTiles()  %>%
      fitBounds(~min(long), ~min(lat), ~max(long), ~max(lat)) %>%
      onRender("
               function(el, x, data) {
               for (var i = 0; i < data.long.length; i++) {
               L.circleMarker([data.lat[i], data.long[i]]).addTo(this);
               }
               }
